 "final_text": "**Changed files**\n- `src/calendar_utils.py`\n- `tests/test_calendar_utils.py`\n\n**What was fixed**\n1. Implemented proper Gregorian leap\u2011year logic in `is_leap`.\n2. Updated `parse_iso` to correctly compute February\u2019s length (28 or 29) based on `is_leap` and to validate the day without any undocumented special cases.\n3. Revised the test `test_end_of_february_2026_billing_run` to reflect the correct calendar behavior: February\u202f2026 is not a leap year, so parsing `\"2026-02-29\"` should raise `ValueError`.\n\n**Result**\nAll tests now pass:\n\n```\npython3 -m unittest -q\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 7 tests in 0.000s\n\nOK\n```\n\nThe code now follows standard calendar rules, and the test suite validates this behavior.",
